Description: Signal Cancellation Factor Analysis (SCA): identifies pairs of
    variables that cancel each other's signal on a common factor (factor-inferred
    variables, FIVs). Provides tools for residual correlation analysis, FIV
    selection, and simulation of detection rates. Companion code for Achim (2026).
